WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.330 --> 00:00:01.980
- [Mark] LD, where'd you grow up?

00:00:03.400 --> 00:00:08.400
- Mostly in Washington, DC
area, Alexandria, Virginia.

00:00:09.890 --> 00:00:12.473
I was born in Eritrea, Asmara.

00:00:13.480 --> 00:00:17.457
Same place, you've heard about
the rapper, Nipsey Hussle?

00:00:17.457 --> 00:00:18.290
- [Mark] Yes.
- Yeah,

00:00:18.290 --> 00:00:19.643
we're from the same country.

00:00:19.643 --> 00:00:20.476
- [Mark] Okay.

00:00:20.476 --> 00:00:21.495
- Part of Ethiopia.

00:00:21.495 --> 00:00:23.600
- [Mark] Oh, is that right?

00:00:23.600 --> 00:00:25.133
And you came to the US when?

00:00:25.133 --> 00:00:28.720
- When I was about five years old.

00:00:28.720 --> 00:00:32.130
My mom brought us over, they
were having a civil war,

00:00:32.130 --> 00:00:36.770
so we had to sneak out
and she walked us...

00:00:36.770 --> 00:00:41.160
She was maybe 21 and she had three kids

00:00:41.160 --> 00:00:45.520
and she moved from Eritrea
to Sudan through the desert.

00:00:45.520 --> 00:00:49.680
And my first two years...

00:00:49.680 --> 00:00:50.850
I mean the next two years,

00:00:50.850 --> 00:00:53.470
we lived in a refugee camp in Sudan.

00:00:53.470 --> 00:00:54.660
- [Mark] And then you
eventually came to DC?

00:00:54.660 --> 00:00:56.580
- Mm-hmm. Yeah.

00:00:56.580 --> 00:01:01.580
- [Mark] And when did the
gang life start for you?

00:01:02.640 --> 00:01:04.373
- It started in DC.

00:01:05.570 --> 00:01:07.360
In high school we had
little cliques, you know,

00:01:07.360 --> 00:01:09.640
things that we'd clique up,

00:01:09.640 --> 00:01:12.380
meaning we got a group of guys together

00:01:12.380 --> 00:01:14.363
and we'd watch each other's back.

00:01:15.330 --> 00:01:16.830
We didn't take it too seriously,

00:01:16.830 --> 00:01:18.360
but you know if somebody
messed with somebody,

00:01:18.360 --> 00:01:21.040
it was automatic we
would back each other up.

00:01:21.040 --> 00:01:22.610
I didn't know anything about gangs

00:01:22.610 --> 00:01:25.069
except for what had I seen
in movies and TV shows.

00:01:25.069 --> 00:01:26.592
- [Mark] They don't exist in Eritrea?

00:01:26.592 --> 00:01:28.200
- No, no.

00:01:28.200 --> 00:01:31.730
They do but not like
they do here in America,

00:01:31.730 --> 00:01:32.823
real organized.

00:01:33.890 --> 00:01:36.463
And then we moved to LA when I was 14.

00:01:39.300 --> 00:01:44.300
And yeah, we moved to
Venice Shoreline Area

00:01:46.390 --> 00:01:50.650
and I was kinda excited about these guys,

00:01:50.650 --> 00:01:52.688
they called himself the Shoreline Crips.

00:01:52.688 --> 00:01:54.057
- [Mark] Yeah, those gangs in Venice.

00:01:54.057 --> 00:01:54.890
- Yeah.

00:01:54.890 --> 00:01:55.920
Yeah, it was crazy,

00:01:55.920 --> 00:01:59.870
'cause for me it was such a
nice area and there's a beach.

00:01:59.870 --> 00:02:00.900
- [Mark] And it's expensive.

00:02:00.900 --> 00:02:01.733
- Yeah, it's expensive.

00:02:01.733 --> 00:02:02.566
- [Mark] Except where it's not.

00:02:02.566 --> 00:02:05.150
- Yeah and I was like how
do they, what's going on?

00:02:05.150 --> 00:02:07.760
Because on the East coast it's,

00:02:07.760 --> 00:02:10.950
the bad areas are really
tight and you can tell.

00:02:10.950 --> 00:02:15.270
Out here, the areas that are gang related,

00:02:15.270 --> 00:02:16.360
you would never know.

00:02:16.360 --> 00:02:18.540
They got nice homes and
everyone got a home.

00:02:18.540 --> 00:02:19.373
- [Mark] Right down the street.

00:02:19.373 --> 00:02:20.240
- Yeah.

00:02:20.240 --> 00:02:23.180
We had a outstanding
apartment most of my life,

00:02:23.180 --> 00:02:26.040
but yeah, I got hooked to that quick.

00:02:26.040 --> 00:02:31.040
I got hooked to the
attention I got in school

00:02:32.110 --> 00:02:34.890
which is weird 'cause in high
school, back in Virginia,

00:02:34.890 --> 00:02:36.750
if you played sports, you got attention.

00:02:36.750 --> 00:02:41.750
Out here, gang members were
like low key, you know, popular.

00:02:41.880 --> 00:02:44.580
Like, everyone respected
them, wanted to be like them.

00:02:45.530 --> 00:02:47.880
And I just wanted to do the same.

00:02:47.880 --> 00:02:49.790
I had two sisters growing up.

00:02:49.790 --> 00:02:51.910
I had little feminine characteristics.

00:02:51.910 --> 00:02:52.940
I didn't like about myself.

00:02:52.940 --> 00:02:55.500
I was really small, under size.

00:02:55.500 --> 00:03:00.500
And I learned how to at
first talk and you know,

00:03:01.360 --> 00:03:04.640
how to communicate
violently, aggressively,

00:03:04.640 --> 00:03:07.240
make fun of people
because I couldn't fight.

00:03:07.240 --> 00:03:10.170
And then I started
getting bigger, stronger,

00:03:10.170 --> 00:03:15.077
and I still wanted to join other people.

00:03:15.077 --> 00:03:18.400
'Cause I didn't think I
could do shit by myself.

00:03:18.400 --> 00:03:21.260
I mean, not to say that all
gang members are like that.

00:03:21.260 --> 00:03:23.670
But for me, honestly,
when I was at that age

00:03:23.670 --> 00:03:26.200
that's what I was, I was
just trying to survive.

00:03:26.200 --> 00:03:28.180
- [Mark] Right.
- Yeah.

00:03:28.180 --> 00:03:33.180
So I dropped, I don't know
if you call it dropped out

00:03:33.590 --> 00:03:35.850
but almost made it to my senior year,

00:03:35.850 --> 00:03:40.850
I failed my senior year
but I went to night school.

00:03:41.503 --> 00:03:43.820
It's like a alternative school,

00:03:43.820 --> 00:03:45.406
where all the girls are pregnant,

00:03:45.406 --> 00:03:47.580
all the other kids on parole, probation,

00:03:47.580 --> 00:03:48.413
something like that.

00:03:48.413 --> 00:03:50.620
I still had never touched the police.

00:03:50.620 --> 00:03:52.080
Actually, one time I did.

00:03:52.080 --> 00:03:53.610
Me and these two kids,

00:03:53.610 --> 00:03:56.220
we were walking back
from the football game.

00:03:56.220 --> 00:03:57.960
I grew up with these two kids

00:03:57.960 --> 00:04:00.750
and they jumped on these two older girls.

00:04:00.750 --> 00:04:02.860
And we used to call it humping,

00:04:02.860 --> 00:04:04.200
where they just would just grab them

00:04:04.200 --> 00:04:05.710
and pull them in to them.

00:04:05.710 --> 00:04:08.050
And we were in what sixth grade.

00:04:08.050 --> 00:04:11.480
And the girls were like
10th, 11th graders.

00:04:11.480 --> 00:04:14.480
Coming to find out those girls
were my sister's best friend.

00:04:15.580 --> 00:04:19.040
We had to go to a hearing
where I asked the girls.

00:04:19.040 --> 00:04:21.327
I was like, "You know I
wasn't part of it, you know.

00:04:21.327 --> 00:04:22.340
"It was those two."

00:04:22.340 --> 00:04:24.350
And they were like, "No, you did it too."

00:04:24.350 --> 00:04:28.440
And that just created the first
shift in my family with me.

00:04:28.440 --> 00:04:30.880
My sister stopped talking to me, really.

00:04:30.880 --> 00:04:34.900
My mom was, she kind of
looked at me differently.

00:04:34.900 --> 00:04:37.580
And I thought, as a kid, I
thought I had raped somebody

00:04:37.580 --> 00:04:40.110
even though I hadn't done nothing.

00:04:40.110 --> 00:04:43.610
I really felt like I was a
rape, you know, like a rapist.

00:04:43.610 --> 00:04:46.930
And I just kind of lived
with that shame and guilt.

00:04:46.930 --> 00:04:50.250
And then by joining the gang,

00:04:50.250 --> 00:04:54.030
when I joined the Crips out in Venice

00:04:54.030 --> 00:04:56.140
that kind of stuff was
talked about so freely.

00:04:56.140 --> 00:04:58.700
And you know, people talked about stripes

00:04:58.700 --> 00:05:02.370
and things they did that most
people would be ashamed of

00:05:02.370 --> 00:05:04.740
or wouldn't want to speak on.

00:05:04.740 --> 00:05:09.740
And over there you got credit
for doing things like that.

00:05:10.320 --> 00:05:12.210
And it made me feel good, basically.

00:05:12.210 --> 00:05:14.400
I felt good about the mistakes I made

00:05:14.400 --> 00:05:17.723
and which were actually
assets for the gang.

00:05:19.040 --> 00:05:23.443
What I brought to the Crips
was I was a master thief.

00:05:24.520 --> 00:05:26.680
I didn't want to do deal with drugs.

00:05:26.680 --> 00:05:28.230
I was always scared to do drugs

00:05:29.160 --> 00:05:30.960
until obviously later on down the road.

00:05:30.960 --> 00:05:33.430
But I just, I was a thief

00:05:33.430 --> 00:05:38.430
and I just hit heists and
licks with different groups,

00:05:39.720 --> 00:05:42.510
different members, different
members all over LA.

00:05:42.510 --> 00:05:46.002
I was small. I was agile,
I could get into places.

00:05:46.002 --> 00:05:49.433
- [Mark] So when you say
(indistinct) what type?

00:05:52.140 --> 00:05:54.550
Persons or-
- No, no, no, no, no.

00:05:54.550 --> 00:05:55.680
- [Mark] Jewelry stores.
- Yeah.

00:05:55.680 --> 00:05:59.590
We would hit stores.
We'd hit armored trucks.

00:05:59.590 --> 00:06:00.940
I mean, a lot of stuff we hit

00:06:00.940 --> 00:06:03.060
you'd never hear about it on the news.

00:06:03.060 --> 00:06:05.800
I think one thing we
did that I was a part of

00:06:06.780 --> 00:06:08.137
I heard about on the news.

00:06:08.137 --> 00:06:13.137
But we hit some a 10,000,
a $20,000 garage full

00:06:14.640 --> 00:06:17.810
of some kind of whatever it had in it.

00:06:17.810 --> 00:06:21.380
Either electronics or something
like a manager had it.

00:06:21.380 --> 00:06:24.040
And it's a lot of money for

00:06:24.040 --> 00:06:27.773
less than an hour's
worth of work and yeah.

00:06:30.340 --> 00:06:33.730
How I eventually started
getting caught up was

00:06:33.730 --> 00:06:34.660
I started getting high.

00:06:34.660 --> 00:06:39.040
I started with weed or
alcohol and weed, obviously,

00:06:39.040 --> 00:06:42.932
little party drugs but I
eventually started doing cocaine

00:06:42.932 --> 00:06:44.183
then I went to crack.

00:06:45.100 --> 00:06:48.090
And once I went to crack, I
lost all respect from everybody.

00:06:48.090 --> 00:06:51.910
All the homies, family.

00:06:51.910 --> 00:06:53.850
And the cocaine was cool
because everyone's like,

00:06:53.850 --> 00:06:56.370
oh, you know, you could
do cocaine, sniff it.

00:06:56.370 --> 00:06:59.670
But once I started doing crack
no one wanted to talk to me

00:06:59.670 --> 00:07:04.040
and I instantly became
"like a crack head".

00:07:04.040 --> 00:07:09.040
Like I didn't have a in between
where I was just struggling.

00:07:11.800 --> 00:07:14.600
I went from nothing to...

00:07:17.120 --> 00:07:18.520
It's weird 'cause the first,

00:07:20.230 --> 00:07:22.550
this homeless guy taught me how to hustle.

00:07:22.550 --> 00:07:24.000
He said, let's recycle cans.

00:07:24.000 --> 00:07:25.310
And I was like, all right, let's do that.

00:07:25.310 --> 00:07:26.730
So I started recycling cans.

00:07:26.730 --> 00:07:30.360
A guy who could steal, who
could do all these things,

00:07:30.360 --> 00:07:32.087
I just figured, you
know, I'll recycle cans

00:07:32.087 --> 00:07:33.650
'cause this guy knows.

00:07:33.650 --> 00:07:34.860
So I did that for a long time.

00:07:34.860 --> 00:07:39.610
I didn't even steal for a while
but once I started stealing,

00:07:39.610 --> 00:07:41.870
I started getting caught because you know,

00:07:41.870 --> 00:07:44.840
I'd go into stores,
looking shabby, sweating,

00:07:44.840 --> 00:07:46.330
as I'm sweating now.

00:07:46.330 --> 00:07:50.110
All skinny, sucked in
face, anxious, you know?

00:07:50.110 --> 00:07:50.943
- [Mark] You could tell.

00:07:50.943 --> 00:07:54.610
- Yeah. You could smell
me from a thousand feet.

00:07:54.610 --> 00:07:57.190
And if you couldn't, I could take a shower

00:07:57.190 --> 00:07:58.770
and put on all brand new clothes

00:07:58.770 --> 00:08:01.250
and be walking with a nice poodle.

00:08:01.250 --> 00:08:02.950
My head is telling me, you could see me.

00:08:02.950 --> 00:08:04.770
So I'm paranoid either
way. I'ma fuck it up...

00:08:04.770 --> 00:08:06.640
So, I started getting into
all these petty thefts

00:08:06.640 --> 00:08:09.930
and you know then that cycle
just kept going and going

00:08:09.930 --> 00:08:12.423
in and out of drug and alcohol programs.

00:08:13.760 --> 00:08:17.640
In between I started
learning how to sell dope.

00:08:17.640 --> 00:08:19.490
Figured if I sell dope, it's a lot easier

00:08:19.490 --> 00:08:22.810
'cause I get it from the hood
and I could take it anywhere

00:08:22.810 --> 00:08:25.160
and I don't have to have
a front, nothing that...

00:08:25.160 --> 00:08:26.890
It's just magic, you can
just go (blows raspberry)

00:08:26.890 --> 00:08:28.567
Someone just gives you
a big pile and he says,

00:08:28.567 --> 00:08:29.790
"Give me this amount of money."

00:08:29.790 --> 00:08:31.120
You're like, "Shit."

00:08:31.120 --> 00:08:34.543
But for a drug addict like me
to have that amount of money,

00:08:35.500 --> 00:08:36.570
(sighs)
- [Mark] Dangerous.

00:08:36.570 --> 00:08:37.403
- Yeah. Dangerous.

00:08:37.403 --> 00:08:40.320
I almost got killed a couple of times

00:08:40.320 --> 00:08:44.330
but luckily the big,
big, big homies knew me

00:08:44.330 --> 00:08:45.163
from when I was a kid.

00:08:45.163 --> 00:08:46.790
And I brought in a lot, I guess I brought

00:08:46.790 --> 00:08:50.220
in a lot more money than I
thought doing these things.

00:08:50.220 --> 00:08:52.173
So I was valuable to them in some way.

00:08:53.290 --> 00:08:55.373
I mean, I smoked up one time.

00:08:56.630 --> 00:09:00.590
I was supposed to bring back $10,000,

00:09:00.590 --> 00:09:05.590
I brought back 1000 and I had
the audacity to come back.

00:09:08.100 --> 00:09:11.127
And I was weird, I talked
differently, you know.

00:09:12.550 --> 00:09:16.300
The way I speak now is how
I spoke there back then.

00:09:16.300 --> 00:09:20.260
And I just had a way of like,
you know, making people laugh

00:09:20.260 --> 00:09:22.830
or do something, you know,
flipping the script about things.

00:09:22.830 --> 00:09:26.210
But you know, once you
start really hitting it

00:09:26.210 --> 00:09:29.340
like I was hitting it, you start mumbling.

00:09:29.340 --> 00:09:33.433
The words don't come out,
you look pitiful, yeah.

00:09:34.270 --> 00:09:36.030
- [Mark] Did you do prison time?

00:09:36.030 --> 00:09:38.325
- [LD] No prison. That's
another crazy thing.

00:09:38.325 --> 00:09:39.158
- [Mark] You've never been in prison?

00:09:39.158 --> 00:09:40.285
- [LD] Never been in prison.

00:09:40.285 --> 00:09:41.970
- [Mark] (indistinct)

00:09:41.970 --> 00:09:44.760
- [LD] I've been to jail a lot of times.

00:09:44.760 --> 00:09:48.530
And like again, when I go to court,

00:09:48.530 --> 00:09:49.790
I don't know if this makes a difference

00:09:49.790 --> 00:09:52.220
but my mom used to tell
us this back, you know

00:09:52.220 --> 00:09:53.662
being immigrants and all

00:09:53.662 --> 00:09:56.150
and not knowing how to speak English.

00:09:56.150 --> 00:10:00.087
She said, "Look, you see the white people?

00:10:00.087 --> 00:10:01.183
"Dress like them, talk like them."

00:10:01.183 --> 00:10:02.990
I'm like, "All right, okay."

00:10:02.990 --> 00:10:04.270
So, I mean, and we grew up

00:10:04.270 --> 00:10:05.870
around a lot of white people in Virginia.

00:10:05.870 --> 00:10:07.390
So I knew all their mannerisms,

00:10:07.390 --> 00:10:09.130
I knew how to present myself.

00:10:09.130 --> 00:10:10.950
So in court, I always
presented myself a totally

00:10:10.950 --> 00:10:12.020
different person.

00:10:12.020 --> 00:10:15.330
And I guess I just got, well
basically I just got lucky.

00:10:15.330 --> 00:10:16.800
Because I mean, I still had a rap sheet

00:10:16.800 --> 00:10:17.988
of all these petty thefts and-

00:10:17.988 --> 00:10:19.300
- [Mark] (indistinct)

00:10:19.300 --> 00:10:21.333
- It does when you're respectful,

00:10:22.670 --> 00:10:25.110
even though I was not feeling respectful

00:10:25.110 --> 00:10:30.110
towards the system and the
criminal courts, I could fake it.

00:10:31.200 --> 00:10:34.810
I was a really good
actor, really good actor,

00:10:34.810 --> 00:10:38.730
which, you know, (indistinct) was trying

00:10:38.730 --> 00:10:41.509
to get me to do acting and shit like that.

00:10:41.509 --> 00:10:42.943
They're like, "Motherfucker, you know,

00:10:42.943 --> 00:10:44.857
"you're not made for this life.

00:10:44.857 --> 00:10:46.390
"You're just forcing yourself."

00:10:46.390 --> 00:10:49.530
And it's true. I was just
forcing myself through it

00:10:49.530 --> 00:10:51.070
but I love the gangs.

00:10:51.070 --> 00:10:53.810
I love everything that they
brought for me, did for me.

00:10:53.810 --> 00:10:56.190
I hated some of the things we had to do,

00:10:56.190 --> 00:10:59.820
the things I had I witnessed, you know,

00:10:59.820 --> 00:11:03.940
girls, women getting raped and
motherfuckers just laughing

00:11:03.940 --> 00:11:06.150
and you know just (blows raspberry)

00:11:06.150 --> 00:11:08.250
The next day you see everybody, what's up?

00:11:09.470 --> 00:11:12.970
I mean, if you knew
how much that happened,

00:11:12.970 --> 00:11:16.900
you'd just think like
it was a rite of passage

00:11:16.900 --> 00:11:17.733
in the neighborhood.

00:11:17.733 --> 00:11:19.373
Like, the women all had to get raped.

00:11:20.890 --> 00:11:23.633
I didn't know one girl
who hadn't been raped.

00:11:25.670 --> 00:11:30.670
Maybe if she was so fly
that everyone fucking,

00:11:30.680 --> 00:11:31.840
you know what I'm saying?

00:11:31.840 --> 00:11:34.730
Or she had a big brother or,
you know what I'm saying?

00:11:34.730 --> 00:11:38.360
Like that, but the even
ones with the big brother,

00:11:38.360 --> 00:11:41.430
like, you know, somebody got them.

00:11:41.430 --> 00:11:44.180
All the girls I grew up
with all, all been raped.

00:11:44.180 --> 00:11:45.840
I know that.

00:11:45.840 --> 00:11:47.760
So I didn't like all
that stuff because I grew

00:11:47.760 --> 00:11:49.810
up with my mom and sisters
and stuff like that.

00:11:49.810 --> 00:11:52.540
But the violence too, you know,

00:11:52.540 --> 00:11:55.210
they tried to toughened
me, change me to be,

00:11:55.210 --> 00:11:56.260
you know, witness shit.

00:11:56.260 --> 00:11:59.840
I saw some I can't ever not see.

00:11:59.840 --> 00:12:04.810
And I knew I had to do some
that I will go to my grave

00:12:04.810 --> 00:12:08.917
with that changed me from the inside out.

00:12:17.570 --> 00:12:21.233
But on the flip side you got this family.

00:12:22.320 --> 00:12:25.323
I had a real family, but
not like this family.

00:12:28.680 --> 00:12:31.530
It's hard to describe what it
meant and what it is to me.

00:12:32.860 --> 00:12:34.130
I was one of the weird...

00:12:34.130 --> 00:12:36.510
I ain't care about my
color, all that shit.

00:12:36.510 --> 00:12:38.390
I just cared about who was
in front of me right there

00:12:38.390 --> 00:12:39.223
and then.

00:12:41.700 --> 00:12:43.970
Gang life to me is family life.

00:12:43.970 --> 00:12:45.770
- [Mark] Do you still feel that way?

00:12:56.470 --> 00:12:57.563
- I can't say I do.

00:12:59.299 --> 00:13:00.991
I mean, it's still family, gang...

00:13:00.991 --> 00:13:02.920
They still there for me, they try,

00:13:02.920 --> 00:13:06.060
but as I gotten older and shit, you know,

00:13:06.060 --> 00:13:07.630
doing things differently,

00:13:07.630 --> 00:13:09.750
they don't even know
how to be there for me.

00:13:09.750 --> 00:13:13.230
They try but they ain't
showing up at events

00:13:13.230 --> 00:13:16.140
or helping me with that
I really need help with.

00:13:16.140 --> 00:13:18.520
They might say, "Here,
here's a thousand dollars."

00:13:18.520 --> 00:13:21.400
Or "Here, take this sack of this and..."

00:13:21.400 --> 00:13:24.410
I can't do that, I'm trying
to do things this way

00:13:24.410 --> 00:13:26.320
and which you know what I'm saying?

00:13:26.320 --> 00:13:27.670
They do the best they can to help

00:13:27.670 --> 00:13:31.423
but it seems like when I first got out,

00:13:32.850 --> 00:13:37.850
really I got out 'cause I was
diagnosed positive with HIV

00:13:37.870 --> 00:13:41.240
and that kind of shook me and
I was trying to commit suicide

00:13:42.230 --> 00:13:43.580
and people just, you know what I'm saying?

00:13:43.580 --> 00:13:45.820
I just talked to the talk to the OGs.

00:13:45.820 --> 00:13:49.460
And was like, "This is
it. I'ma commit suicide."

00:13:49.460 --> 00:13:52.360
And all right motherfucker you
gotta do what you gotta do.

00:13:52.360 --> 00:13:54.773
Go ahead. You know,
our blessings, you out.

00:13:55.880 --> 00:13:58.480
And I really did think I
was gonna commit suicide

00:13:58.480 --> 00:14:02.750
but I ended up not taking medications.

00:14:02.750 --> 00:14:04.183
Things change over time.

00:14:06.770 --> 00:14:10.477
- [Mark] Where do you
think you contracted HIV?

00:14:10.477 --> 00:14:12.343
- Having sex without condoms.

00:14:13.660 --> 00:14:16.120
During my addiction I did a lot of things

00:14:16.120 --> 00:14:20.369
for money that men don't
like to talk about.

00:14:20.369 --> 00:14:22.900
But yeah, especially in the early years

00:14:22.900 --> 00:14:26.253
where I had no control over
(indistinct) it was a monster.

00:14:28.860 --> 00:14:33.290
One time I stayed up at 30 days
straight, 30 days straight.

00:14:33.290 --> 00:14:35.457
I know meth addicts who've
never stayed up that long.

00:14:35.457 --> 00:14:36.320
- [Mark] This is crack?

00:14:36.320 --> 00:14:38.580
- On crack on crack.
- [Mark] 30 days?

00:14:38.580 --> 00:14:41.953
- Yeah, 30 days straight on
crack. I was much younger.

00:14:45.080 --> 00:14:46.483
Yeah. It had a hold of me.

00:14:48.910 --> 00:14:53.910
Yeah, I think it's family
but not a true real family.

00:14:55.505 --> 00:14:56.880
- [Mark] (indistinct)

00:14:56.880 --> 00:14:59.850
- Yeah, no, no, we don't
have nothing like that.

00:14:59.850 --> 00:15:03.760
You know, you gotta have a
real hard stomach and you know,

00:15:03.760 --> 00:15:05.790
it started like that
for me even growing up

00:15:05.790 --> 00:15:07.473
in Sudan, watching some shit.

00:15:08.495 --> 00:15:12.940
I saw girls who were my age having sex

00:15:12.940 --> 00:15:14.493
and getting raped in Sudan.

00:15:16.335 --> 00:15:18.130
- [Mark] Which was how old?

00:15:18.130 --> 00:15:20.483
- I was like five, four or five.

00:15:21.420 --> 00:15:25.970
I used to see people's heads
get chopped off, arms, limbs.

00:15:25.970 --> 00:15:26.950
Just in the street right there.

00:15:26.950 --> 00:15:30.200
I remember just staring
at body parts and...

00:15:30.200 --> 00:15:32.770
I mean, I guess I was
conditioned for this life,

00:15:32.770 --> 00:15:35.930
from beginning, you know.

00:15:35.930 --> 00:15:38.370
I wasn't much for getting queasy

00:15:38.370 --> 00:15:41.150
but participating wasn't
my thing in that area.

00:15:41.150 --> 00:15:42.207
But I knew I wanted to be a part of it

00:15:42.207 --> 00:15:45.756
'cause it seemed like a powerful
thing especially in Sudan.

00:15:45.756 --> 00:15:48.050
I remember I looked up to them,

00:15:48.050 --> 00:15:51.729
I looked up to all of the
bigger boys running around.

00:15:51.729 --> 00:15:53.983
They pretty much ran shit so, yeah.

00:15:55.830 --> 00:15:57.150
- [Mark] Do you think
that coming to America

00:15:57.150 --> 00:16:00.823
is something that helped you in a way?

00:16:01.700 --> 00:16:02.533
How do you view it?

00:16:02.533 --> 00:16:03.680
- You know, my mom always says this thing.

00:16:03.680 --> 00:16:05.330
She goes, "You know I
brought you all the way here

00:16:05.330 --> 00:16:07.600
from Africa for this?"

00:16:07.600 --> 00:16:09.607
She goes, "America's fucked up."

00:16:11.041 --> 00:16:12.640
I mean, she says it in
a different kind of way

00:16:12.640 --> 00:16:14.150
but that's basically what she means.

00:16:14.150 --> 00:16:15.147
She's like, "How could you go all the way

00:16:15.147 --> 00:16:16.697
"from Africa to Skid Row?"

00:16:17.860 --> 00:16:19.960
She goes, "Skid Row is the
worst thing I've ever seen."

00:16:19.960 --> 00:16:22.267
She goes, "There's people
who don't even have shoes

00:16:22.267 --> 00:16:25.490
"in Eritrea who live better
than people in Skid Row."

00:16:25.490 --> 00:16:28.740
I mean, she didn't mean
better like clothes-wise

00:16:28.740 --> 00:16:31.125
but just, you know-

00:16:31.125 --> 00:16:31.958
- [Mark] Healthier, safer, life.

00:16:31.958 --> 00:16:34.180
- Healthier, safer life, yeah.

00:16:34.180 --> 00:16:37.550
My mom's from a war torn land.

00:16:37.550 --> 00:16:40.610
She walked through three
weeks through a desert.

00:16:40.610 --> 00:16:41.780
I died in her hands.

00:16:41.780 --> 00:16:44.710
She walked with me for
two days with a dead body.

00:16:44.710 --> 00:16:47.150
And then miraculously I came back to life.

00:16:47.150 --> 00:16:48.449
She was like-

00:16:48.449 --> 00:16:49.282
- [Mark] What was that about?

00:16:49.282 --> 00:16:51.550
- I don't know, but I'm a miracle baby.

00:16:51.550 --> 00:16:53.930
She said we were on this
military bus walking

00:16:53.930 --> 00:16:56.880
through the desert, the military
bus came and picked us up.

00:16:58.640 --> 00:17:00.150
He's thinking, we're gonna kick him...

00:17:00.150 --> 00:17:01.370
We're gonna throw his body over.

00:17:01.370 --> 00:17:02.700
My mom was like, "No."

00:17:02.700 --> 00:17:04.059
She held onto me for a little longer

00:17:04.059 --> 00:17:06.073
and I guess I came alive.

00:17:07.860 --> 00:17:12.740
She was, my oldest sister
she had when she was 12.

00:17:12.740 --> 00:17:15.820
So I think she was only
like 16, 17 at the time.

00:17:15.820 --> 00:17:17.260
I don't know, something really young.

00:17:17.260 --> 00:17:18.093
- [Mark] Your mom?

00:17:18.093 --> 00:17:20.280
- She was really young,
yeah. When she did that trek.

00:17:20.280 --> 00:17:22.100
So she's seen a lot of shit.

00:17:22.100 --> 00:17:23.940
The women fight wars over there.

00:17:23.940 --> 00:17:26.940
But when she came to Skid Row
and seen how I've been living,

00:17:27.990 --> 00:17:28.823
she couldn't handle it.

00:17:28.823 --> 00:17:30.207
She's like, "This is worse than any place

00:17:30.207 --> 00:17:31.340
"in Africa I've ever seen."

00:17:31.340 --> 00:17:33.180
- [Mark] Where does your mom live now?

00:17:33.180 --> 00:17:34.910
- She's still in Virginia, yeah.

00:17:34.910 --> 00:17:38.390
She's coming over here a
couple of times looking for me,

00:17:38.390 --> 00:17:39.410
especially in the earlier days

00:17:39.410 --> 00:17:44.316
when I was just like
straight street gutter.

00:17:44.316 --> 00:17:46.199
- [Mark] Are you using today?

00:17:46.199 --> 00:17:49.800
- Today, I mean, I use
occasionally but not...

00:17:51.140 --> 00:17:55.713
I have a place to live
today, it's just different.

00:17:58.290 --> 00:17:59.530
I have been up a couple of days

00:17:59.530 --> 00:18:01.660
because the first of the month,
a lot of people have money.

00:18:01.660 --> 00:18:04.090
So, you just go around
and get high for free.

00:18:04.090 --> 00:18:06.900
But it's not an everyday thing.

00:18:06.900 --> 00:18:09.150
I mean, I had a real good job recently

00:18:09.150 --> 00:18:12.010
for a couple of years, I
was working in treatment.

00:18:12.010 --> 00:18:15.533
But I lost that due to relapse.

00:18:17.550 --> 00:18:21.500
Yeah. But you know, I could
keep a phone once in a while.

00:18:21.500 --> 00:18:24.323
You know what I mean? I'm
doing enough to survive.

00:18:25.355 --> 00:18:30.355
- [Mark] What's the worst thing
that's ever happened to you?

00:18:31.799 --> 00:18:34.466
- Being here as a demission and-

00:18:35.891 --> 00:18:37.224
- [Mark] Which is
probably a result of being

00:18:37.224 --> 00:18:38.438
on crack.
- Yeah, yeah.

00:18:38.438 --> 00:18:39.360
- [Mark] So being on crack is really

00:18:39.360 --> 00:18:40.250
the worst thing that's ever happened?

00:18:40.250 --> 00:18:42.260
- Well, yeah, there's
a guy who worked there

00:18:42.260 --> 00:18:45.800
who was one of my roommates
there and I relapsed, right?

00:18:45.800 --> 00:18:48.970
And then the next day I,
I used a little longer.

00:18:48.970 --> 00:18:50.860
I take one hit and I lose like 20 pounds.

00:18:50.860 --> 00:18:52.630
I think I saw him a couple of weeks later

00:18:52.630 --> 00:18:55.060
and he's a big guy, way bigger than me.

00:18:55.060 --> 00:18:56.880
And he held me at knife point.

00:18:56.880 --> 00:18:59.080
He took me to this house,

00:18:59.080 --> 00:19:00.430
we were supposed to do
something for money.

00:19:00.430 --> 00:19:03.260
I was like, "Nah, I ain't do nothing, OG."

00:19:03.260 --> 00:19:08.090
And he had a knife and
a gun and he raped me

00:19:08.090 --> 00:19:10.270
and I had never had sex.

00:19:10.270 --> 00:19:15.270
And he was open about his AIDS status.

00:19:16.270 --> 00:19:18.890
And honestly, that that's
really where I think I,

00:19:18.890 --> 00:19:20.870
where I know I got it.

00:19:20.870 --> 00:19:23.000
I like to say just sex without condoms.

00:19:23.000 --> 00:19:25.190
'Cause it makes me sound like,
you know what I'm saying?

00:19:25.190 --> 00:19:27.530
Irresponsible, gigolo or something.

00:19:27.530 --> 00:19:29.020
But no,

00:19:29.020 --> 00:19:31.960
that's probably the worst
thing that ever happened to me.

00:19:31.960 --> 00:19:36.173
It took a while for me to stop
thinking about killing him.

00:19:37.860 --> 00:19:42.030
But I couldn't stop because I kept using.

00:19:42.030 --> 00:19:44.120
And when you're using the
last thing you wanna do

00:19:44.120 --> 00:19:45.560
is go take care of any kind of business.

00:19:45.560 --> 00:19:47.700
Even if it means revenge business,

00:19:47.700 --> 00:19:51.213
like, using comes primary to everything.

00:19:55.020 --> 00:19:56.760
Yeah, this last relapse hasn't been as bad

00:19:56.760 --> 00:19:58.460
because I've been able to develop,

00:20:00.190 --> 00:20:04.190
get a foundation, get a place,
live, all these good things.

00:20:04.190 --> 00:20:06.130
And now I'm just trying to hold on to it

00:20:06.130 --> 00:20:11.130
and not try to go to jail
or do anything stupid.

00:20:11.778 --> 00:20:13.630
'Cause you know, I'm old
enough, smart enough.

00:20:13.630 --> 00:20:18.630
I know people, it's easy to
just get a drug if I want it.

00:20:19.880 --> 00:20:21.005
It's not that serious.

00:20:21.005 --> 00:20:23.243
What makes it easier is the drugs suck.

00:20:24.710 --> 00:20:27.000
I mean, they're trying
to kill you, basically.

00:20:27.000 --> 00:20:29.400
Last night, there's one dealer,

00:20:29.400 --> 00:20:31.330
he knows I always have money,

00:20:31.330 --> 00:20:33.200
was mad 'cause I wouldn't buy from him.

00:20:33.200 --> 00:20:38.200
And he laced a crack rock
with some embalming fluid.

00:20:39.160 --> 00:20:42.100
And I thought that was the end for me.

00:20:42.100 --> 00:20:46.130
But for some reason, I
just, I was really strong.

00:20:46.130 --> 00:20:48.500
And some reason I started eating

00:20:48.500 --> 00:20:50.430
and drinking water and boom.

00:20:50.430 --> 00:20:52.000
I don't know, to me it lasted 30 minutes,

00:20:52.000 --> 00:20:53.470
it could have been four or five hours

00:20:53.470 --> 00:20:55.020
but I'm glad I made it through.

00:20:56.630 --> 00:21:00.051
Take a risk out here every
day for just fucking-

00:21:00.051 --> 00:21:01.460
- [Mark] (indistinct)

00:21:01.460 --> 00:21:03.363
- Yeah, yeah. Basically, many times.

00:21:04.593 --> 00:21:09.176
- [Mark] What (indistinct) to go back?

00:21:10.253 --> 00:21:12.810
- It's weird to say,
but it's instant family.

00:21:12.810 --> 00:21:15.760
It's instant community.
It's instant, you know...

00:21:15.760 --> 00:21:18.490
You're a part of something right away.

00:21:18.490 --> 00:21:21.950
You don't have to be work your way.

00:21:21.950 --> 00:21:23.640
I've always liked things fast.

00:21:23.640 --> 00:21:25.550
I come out here and
boom I got a community.

00:21:25.550 --> 00:21:27.650
I could be the leader of
this. I could do this.

00:21:27.650 --> 00:21:29.700
I could be the best at this quick.

00:21:29.700 --> 00:21:32.470
People come and go, you
know what I'm saying?

00:21:32.470 --> 00:21:34.610
As far as real life where it takes

00:21:34.610 --> 00:21:36.590
a long time to develop
relationships with people

00:21:36.590 --> 00:21:39.290
'cause out here we see each
other all day, every day.

00:21:39.290 --> 00:21:40.327
You get a relationship
quick, hey, boom, boom, boom.

00:21:40.327 --> 00:21:42.430
You go to the next one, boom, boom, boom.

00:21:42.430 --> 00:21:44.340
Everything's fast moving.

00:21:44.340 --> 00:21:46.780
I like, you know, I feel alive.

00:21:46.780 --> 00:21:49.240
Like, I haven't been on the
phone for like three months.

00:21:49.240 --> 00:21:51.200
I noticed that yesterday
I was on the train

00:21:51.200 --> 00:21:52.997
and I'm looking at everybody like this.

00:21:52.997 --> 00:21:54.880
I'm like, "Wow. I remember
I used to be like that."

00:21:54.880 --> 00:21:57.240
And I used to feel like
if I wasn't like that

00:21:57.240 --> 00:21:59.740
how am I gonna make it on
this train for the next eight,

00:21:59.740 --> 00:22:00.573
four stops?

00:22:00.573 --> 00:22:02.060
There's no way I can
make it without my phone.

00:22:02.060 --> 00:22:03.990
If my phone dies it's over.

00:22:03.990 --> 00:22:07.530
But now I ride from one line to the end

00:22:07.530 --> 00:22:08.610
and it feels like nothing.

00:22:08.610 --> 00:22:10.240
You know, it's really,

00:22:10.240 --> 00:22:12.490
it has some qualities
to it being homeless.

00:22:12.490 --> 00:22:15.293
And you talk to people,

00:22:16.640 --> 00:22:18.690
you're engaged with the world around you.

00:22:20.660 --> 00:22:22.010
You have no other choice

00:22:22.010 --> 00:22:23.630
or you go crazy and
start talking to yourself

00:22:23.630 --> 00:22:25.005
which is not a (indistinct) to do.

00:22:25.005 --> 00:22:27.020
I don't wanna be that guy.

00:22:27.020 --> 00:22:29.220
If I'm desperate to talk
to somebody, I will.

00:22:29.220 --> 00:22:33.170
I'll go find an old person.
I'll go find a crazy person.

00:22:33.170 --> 00:22:34.040
Yeah. But-

00:22:35.173 --> 00:22:36.876
- [Mark] What do you see for
yourself in next five years.

00:22:36.876 --> 00:22:38.450
Any plans, any goals?

00:22:38.450 --> 00:22:41.527
- Yeah, my plan is to get
a hundred percent sober.

00:22:41.527 --> 00:22:43.250
You know, I know it doesn't work

00:22:43.250 --> 00:22:45.726
trying to do a little
drugs here and there.

00:22:45.726 --> 00:22:50.726
And I don't know, there's no
specific thing I wanna do.

00:22:52.660 --> 00:22:57.660
I just wanna be productive and
be a part of helping society.

00:22:57.670 --> 00:22:59.260
You know, pay taxes, whatever.

00:22:59.260 --> 00:23:02.500
But the hobbies I'd like to participate

00:23:02.500 --> 00:23:06.160
in is just giving back and
being present for young kids

00:23:06.160 --> 00:23:07.740
who are in gangs.

00:23:07.740 --> 00:23:10.740
No message, no, nothing, just there.

00:23:10.740 --> 00:23:12.500
Someone who's made it through,
who's on the other side.

00:23:12.500 --> 00:23:16.940
Just, you know, big brother,
man. having a big brother.

00:23:16.940 --> 00:23:18.307
I always dreamed, I was like,

00:23:18.307 --> 00:23:19.827
"God, please let me have,

00:23:19.827 --> 00:23:21.050
"'cause I don't know how to do this."

00:23:21.050 --> 00:23:22.100
I didn't know how to have sex.

00:23:22.100 --> 00:23:25.981
I had to listen to 10 year
olds tell me how to do this.

00:23:25.981 --> 00:23:28.800
- [Mark] Being a great role model can be

00:23:28.800 --> 00:23:32.258
more powerful than giving
all the advice (indistinct)

00:23:32.258 --> 00:23:34.090
You don't have to say anything

00:23:34.090 --> 00:23:37.040
but just like being that person
that these kids look up to.

00:23:38.875 --> 00:23:39.890
- Yeah.

00:23:39.890 --> 00:23:41.490
- [Mark] That's what you can do.

00:23:43.380 --> 00:23:45.350
- Some of the people,
my best role models were

00:23:45.350 --> 00:23:47.593
who I can't ever remember
our conversations.

00:23:47.593 --> 00:23:48.653
I remember just what they did.

00:23:48.653 --> 00:23:50.180
- [Mark] And you'll never forget it.

00:23:50.180 --> 00:23:52.390
- Never. How they did,
how they did school,

00:23:52.390 --> 00:23:57.180
what he did after school and
I was like, "Damn, that's it."

00:23:57.180 --> 00:23:58.160
- [Mark] Kids don't
listen to their parents,

00:23:58.160 --> 00:23:59.350
they turn into their parents.

00:23:59.350 --> 00:24:01.910
If your parents are stand-up citizens,

00:24:01.910 --> 00:24:03.306
that walked a straight line,

00:24:03.306 --> 00:24:04.357
their kids will do that.
- Exactly.

00:24:04.357 --> 00:24:08.133
- [Mark] But if their parents
were alcoholics, or lazy

00:24:08.133 --> 00:24:12.863
or off-track guaranteed to follow suit.

00:24:13.760 --> 00:24:16.740
- My mom was, funny 'cause
she didn't drink or anything,

00:24:16.740 --> 00:24:18.180
but she was not lazy.

00:24:18.180 --> 00:24:20.580
And they know me as Mr....

00:24:20.580 --> 00:24:23.920
It's impossible for me
to not, or to be lazy.

00:24:23.920 --> 00:24:25.970
Like, a lot of young
brothers siting on the curb

00:24:25.970 --> 00:24:29.850
and play dice and I can't
do that, I just can't.

00:24:29.850 --> 00:24:32.330
I gotta be moving or doing something.

00:24:32.330 --> 00:24:33.900
Even if it means going to help somebody

00:24:33.900 --> 00:24:35.000
do something for free.

00:24:36.500 --> 00:24:41.500
I don't wanna die, you know?
So death to me is stagnation.

00:24:44.220 --> 00:24:47.403
Just sitting there
watching cop cars go by,

00:24:48.340 --> 00:24:50.690
squirming and shit. I wanna live.

00:24:55.227 --> 00:24:56.933
And gangs gave me the best,

00:24:57.920 --> 00:24:59.960
from what I've experienced so far,

00:24:59.960 --> 00:25:02.580
one of the best opportunities like that,

00:25:02.580 --> 00:25:04.540
minus all the other shit we did.

00:25:04.540 --> 00:25:07.613
I really felt alive doing
everything every day I woke up.

00:25:08.540 --> 00:25:13.120
I watched those movies, you
know, De Niro, whatever.

00:25:13.120 --> 00:25:16.010
Some people they get
excited, but I lived it.

00:25:16.010 --> 00:25:17.920
So, I mean, not like,
you know what I mean?

00:25:17.920 --> 00:25:22.620
I wasn't like in
different countries per se

00:25:22.620 --> 00:25:24.610
but I did a lot of exciting shit.

00:25:24.610 --> 00:25:27.803
So, it doesn't impress me to
see other people live that way.

00:25:30.641 --> 00:25:32.810
I just wanna live and now being sober

00:25:32.810 --> 00:25:35.260
or trying to get sober, I
wanna do the same thing.

00:25:35.260 --> 00:25:37.470
I don't wanna be on my phone,

00:25:37.470 --> 00:25:40.940
I wanna be participating in
doing whatever I gotta do to be-

00:25:40.940 --> 00:25:42.250
- [Mark] Did you ever have a relationship

00:25:42.250 --> 00:25:44.400
with somebody where
you were close to them?

00:25:44.400 --> 00:25:46.033
- Yeah. Yeah. I had one.

00:25:47.000 --> 00:25:49.550
I met her when I went back
home to Eritrea to visit

00:25:51.030 --> 00:25:53.470
and she's a beautiful person.

00:25:53.470 --> 00:25:55.610
We had a three-month thing, got married.

00:25:55.610 --> 00:25:56.590
We didn't tell our parents,

00:25:56.590 --> 00:26:01.010
which for that country, our
culture is biggest no-no

00:26:02.390 --> 00:26:03.900
and no one knew about me and her.

00:26:03.900 --> 00:26:08.803
They just knew that Simon the
dude who, I gave my real name,

00:26:09.730 --> 00:26:13.130
the dude who never even fucked with girls

00:26:13.130 --> 00:26:15.750
or had a girlfriend like
that or brought one home,

00:26:15.750 --> 00:26:17.240
all of a sudden, wants to get married

00:26:17.240 --> 00:26:19.350
and is obsessed over this woman.

00:26:19.350 --> 00:26:21.430
And she was awesome.

00:26:21.430 --> 00:26:24.160
She could speak like five languages.

00:26:24.160 --> 00:26:29.160
She, like 5'8", like 110
pounds, beautiful body, perfect.

00:26:30.200 --> 00:26:32.650
And the thing that, I
remember thinking that got me,

00:26:32.650 --> 00:26:35.390
we were at the university
library just talking

00:26:35.390 --> 00:26:39.977
and a bird flew into a wall
and she said, "Hold on."

00:26:39.977 --> 00:26:41.927
And she picked up the bird and she said,

00:26:41.927 --> 00:26:45.400
"Go get me a cup of sugar
and water and mix it up."

00:26:45.400 --> 00:26:47.070
What are you doing?

00:26:47.070 --> 00:26:47.903
She took it.

00:26:47.903 --> 00:26:49.770
She put the sugar water in her mouth

00:26:49.770 --> 00:26:51.310
and fed the bird out of her mouth.

00:26:51.310 --> 00:26:53.170
Then put the bird on her shoulder.

00:26:53.170 --> 00:26:55.137
And she goes, "Come on, keep talking.

00:26:55.137 --> 00:26:58.760
"Watch, in five minutes she'll
have the energy to fly away."

00:26:58.760 --> 00:27:00.230
And she did.

00:27:00.230 --> 00:27:02.810
And this was like a
beautiful model type kind

00:27:02.810 --> 00:27:05.923
of girl wearing these
flip flops with like,

00:27:08.580 --> 00:27:10.557
I was like, "Damn, no woman in America,

00:27:10.557 --> 00:27:15.340
"no girl that I ever ran across
would ever touch an animal."

00:27:15.340 --> 00:27:17.360
And then it just didn't,

00:27:17.360 --> 00:27:20.860
to me she just blew my mind and
she was way smarter than me.

00:27:20.860 --> 00:27:22.810
Philosophy, math.

00:27:22.810 --> 00:27:27.060
She's just do math on top of
her head like ta-da-da-da.

00:27:27.060 --> 00:27:27.920
Yeah, anyway,

00:27:27.920 --> 00:27:30.041
but on top of that we just
connected, we just connected.

00:27:30.041 --> 00:27:32.120
- [Mark] What happened
to that relationship?

00:27:32.120 --> 00:27:35.910
- Me, after I left back to California

00:27:37.770 --> 00:27:39.870
I couldn't do the
paperwork that I needed to

00:27:39.870 --> 00:27:42.240
do to send her over here.

00:27:42.240 --> 00:27:45.530
I couldn't pull off going into an office.

00:27:45.530 --> 00:27:49.042
And so I sit in a corner
somewhere and feel depressed

00:27:49.042 --> 00:27:50.977
and be like "Oh, I can't
do it and I miss her

00:27:50.977 --> 00:27:52.750
"and I love her, but I can't do it."

00:27:52.750 --> 00:27:55.970
Just fucking bullshit, bitch ass shit.

00:27:55.970 --> 00:28:00.240
And one day her uncle came

00:28:00.240 --> 00:28:02.270
and he actually came to where I was at.

00:28:02.270 --> 00:28:04.040
I was like, the only
way this is gonna happen

00:28:04.040 --> 00:28:05.930
is someone needs to come
exactly where I'm at

00:28:05.930 --> 00:28:10.203
at that time to get me to do
this paperwork, it happened.

00:28:11.290 --> 00:28:13.780
And then she stayed with
me like, officially.

00:28:13.780 --> 00:28:15.660
You know, we were still,

00:28:15.660 --> 00:28:20.660
she joined the military
and she's a marksman.

00:28:21.330 --> 00:28:24.950
She can shoot. Everyone in
Eritrea goes to the army.

00:28:24.950 --> 00:28:27.350
So, she's a really good shooter.

00:28:27.350 --> 00:28:30.060
So, she got up with the
general, some dah-dah-dah-dah

00:28:30.060 --> 00:28:31.670
then she started studying about drugs.

00:28:31.670 --> 00:28:33.307
And I remember her on the phone saying,

00:28:33.307 --> 00:28:36.687
"Simon, you know you love this crack shit.

00:28:36.687 --> 00:28:39.137
"You love crack I'm gonna
try crack (indistinct)"

00:28:40.059 --> 00:28:41.290
I was like, "Are you serious?"

00:28:41.290 --> 00:28:42.407
She was like, "Yeah, I wanna try it

00:28:42.407 --> 00:28:47.340
"because if this thing is
more important than me.

00:28:50.507 --> 00:28:52.227
"I wanna enjoy something
that's more important

00:28:52.227 --> 00:28:55.480
"than someone I love.
It must be really good."

00:28:55.480 --> 00:29:00.480
And in a quirky way she
wasn't joking, she would've.

00:29:01.360 --> 00:29:04.610
But then she stayed with me
and she finished her two years

00:29:04.610 --> 00:29:07.060
in the military and I
still couldn't pull it off.

00:29:07.970 --> 00:29:10.760
Our divorce paperwork that
she needed to move on.

00:29:10.760 --> 00:29:12.410
She was going to graduate school.

00:29:14.180 --> 00:29:16.373
She had to fly in from,

00:29:17.460 --> 00:29:21.090
at the time she was in
school in Arizona, somewhere.

00:29:21.090 --> 00:29:24.140
She'd flown in from like
Arizona with a notary

00:29:24.980 --> 00:29:27.970
and the hotel of my choice,

00:29:27.970 --> 00:29:30.833
closest to Skid Row that I
liked, I liked the standard.

00:29:32.970 --> 00:29:34.730
For me to sign the divorce paperwork

00:29:34.730 --> 00:29:37.300
because I couldn't pull
it off any other way.

00:29:37.300 --> 00:29:38.160
She had been trying to do it

00:29:38.160 --> 00:29:40.540
with me for like six or seven months.

00:29:40.540 --> 00:29:42.057
She's like, "Simon, all
you gotta do sign it

00:29:42.057 --> 00:29:44.270
"because and when you do,
I can do this, this, this."

00:29:44.270 --> 00:29:46.120
She wasn't a full citizen yet

00:29:46.120 --> 00:29:48.060
so that that paperwork was real important.

00:29:48.060 --> 00:29:50.860
So she had to fly in that
day come with her notary.

00:29:50.860 --> 00:29:51.920
And that's how stuck I was.

00:29:51.920 --> 00:29:54.500
That's how important drugs were to me.

00:29:54.500 --> 00:29:56.480
- [Mark] How long ago was this?

00:29:56.480 --> 00:30:01.480
- (sighs) 10, let's see,
I'm 40 years old now,

00:30:03.590 --> 00:30:08.560
30, about 15 or 12, something like that.

00:30:08.560 --> 00:30:10.590
I don't even know the dates and times.

00:30:10.590 --> 00:30:13.537
I know everything through my
friends back home who say,

00:30:13.537 --> 00:30:16.037
"Oh yeah, remember you
called me from that program

00:30:16.037 --> 00:30:17.757
"in Arizona, yeah.

00:30:17.757 --> 00:30:21.770
"You did this and they
won the championship."

00:30:21.770 --> 00:30:25.089
I don't know, it's a big blur.

00:30:25.089 --> 00:30:27.290
A lot of it's just a big blur.

00:30:27.290 --> 00:30:28.950
And that's why I liked the life out here

00:30:28.950 --> 00:30:30.842
because it's so hard to give up this life

00:30:30.842 --> 00:30:33.610
because it's a blur.

00:30:33.610 --> 00:30:35.160
It just keeps going the action.

00:30:36.250 --> 00:30:38.350
Even if you're not even a part of it

00:30:38.350 --> 00:30:41.940
you got so many spectators
out here, you know,

00:30:41.940 --> 00:30:43.400
wanna be gang members,

00:30:43.400 --> 00:30:45.350
people who just love to watch the shit.

00:30:46.590 --> 00:30:49.210
They pretend like it's (indistinct)

00:30:49.210 --> 00:30:50.200
motherfuckers are ignorant,

00:30:50.200 --> 00:30:52.740
but they literally are spectators.

00:30:52.740 --> 00:30:54.390
They come out here and get chairs

00:30:55.250 --> 00:30:58.380
and they sit for hours, 10, 12 hours.

00:30:58.380 --> 00:31:00.760
And then they pretend
they have some fake hustle

00:31:00.760 --> 00:31:03.620
like selling candy.
No, they're so excited.

00:31:03.620 --> 00:31:06.973
They wanna do what we do
but they just don't have it.

00:31:11.345 --> 00:31:12.210
- [Mark] All right, man.

00:31:12.210 --> 00:31:13.250
Thank you so much for talking to me.

00:31:13.250 --> 00:31:15.620
- Thank you.
- [Mark] Very interesting.

00:31:15.620 --> 00:31:16.453
Good luck with everything.

00:31:16.453 --> 00:31:17.286
- Thank you.

